{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UyXK7Hs5EwGDy9SYgBCJfo","type":"tool_result","content":"<system-reminder>[Truncated: PARTIAL view — showing lines 1-1341 of 1980 total (31355 tokens, cap 25000). Call Read with offset=1342 limit=1341 for the next page, or Grep to find a specific section. Do NOT answer from this page alone if the answer may be further in the file.]</system-reminder>\n\n1\t#!/usr/bin/env bash\n2\t# harden-core.sh - Harden loop rubric bootstrap + reviewer helpers\n3\t\n4\t# loop-core.sh (the old shared-engine barrel) is deleted; harden-core sources the\n5\t# focused modules it actually uses, each directly and idempotently so it works\n6\t# both through bin/almanac and when a test sources this file directly. core.sh\n7\t# is sourced literally (it owns the helper); the other deps go through\n8\t# _almanac_source_sibling so the boilerplate stays minimal.\n9\tif ! declare -F _error >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n10\t  __harden_core_dir=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd -P)\"\n11\t  # shellcheck source=lib/core.sh\n12\t  source \"$__harden_core_dir/core.sh\"\n13\t  unset __harden_core_dir\n14\tfi\n15\t\n16\t# Explicit deps (each declared module is the contract surface this file consumes;\n17\t# transitive availability is not relied on).\n18\t_almanac_source_sibling agent.sh    almanac_loop_agent_capture   # agent run shapes (ratify/fixer)\n19\t_almanac_source_sibling run.sh      almanac_loop_register_run    # run registry + worker paths/health\n20\t_almanac_source_sibling worker.sh   almanac_loop_worker_start    # worker orchestration (reviewer/fixer fan-out)\n21\t_almanac_source_sibling ui.sh       almanac_loop_ui_render       # gum-or-plain dashboard seam\n22\t_almanac_source_sibling role.sh     almanac_loop_role_config     # per-role provider/model/effort resolution\n23\t_almanac_source_sibling feedback.sh almanac_loop_feedback_run    # objective fixer gate\n24\t\n25\t# --- Role config (per-role provider / model / effort) --------------------------\n26\t#\n27\t# Each harden role selects its own agent config:\n28\t#   conductor - judges/ratifies findings and declares convergence\n29\t#   reviewer  - one read-only reviewer per lens (lens -> provider map)\n30\t#   fixer     - the single sequential write-capable fixer\n31\t#\n32\t# Resolution layers, most specific first, via the shared loop resolver:\n33\t#   provider: HARDEN_<ROLE>[_<LENS>]_PROVIDER -> HARDEN_<ROLE>_PROVIDER\n34\t#             -> HARDEN_PROVIDER -> claude (sensible default: Claude plays every role)\n35\t#   model:    HARDEN_<ROLE>[_<LENS>]_MODEL    -> HARDEN_<ROLE>_MODEL\n36\t#             -> HARDEN_MODEL -> \"\" (the provider's own default)\n37\t#   effort:   HARDEN_<ROLE>[_<LENS>]_EFFORT   -> HARDEN_<ROLE>_EFFORT\n38\t#             -> HARDEN_EFFORT -> \"\" (the provider's own default)\n39\t#\n40\t# Only reviewers consult the lens, so providers can be mixed across lenses in one\n41\t# round; conductor and fixer are single-instance and ignore it. Resolution reads\n42\t# ONLY HARDEN_* (and the shared loop env) — never any host marker — so the tuple\n43\t# is identical whether the run was launched from Claude Code or Codex. Emits three\n44\t# TSV rows (provider/model/effort); returns 2 on an unknown role.\n45\talmanac_harden_role() {\n46\t  local role=\"$1\"\n47\t  local lens=\"${2:-}\"\n48\t\n49\t  case \"$role\" in\n50\t    reviewer) ;;                 # reviewers map lens -> provider\n51\t    conductor | fixer) lens=\"\" ;; # single-instance roles ignore the lens\n52\t    *) return 2 ;;\n53\t  esac\n54\t\n55\t  almanac_loop_role_config \"harden\" \"$role\" \"$lens\" \"$(almanac_provider_default)\" \"\" \"\"\n56\t}\n57\t\n58\t# One field (provider | model | effort) of a harden role's resolved config, for\n59\t# call sites that need a single value. Thin reader over almanac_harden_role so\n60\t# harden's per-role defaults stay defined in exactly one place.\n61\talmanac_harden_role_field() {\n62\t  local role=\"$1\"\n63\t  local field=\"$2\"\n64\t  local lens=\"${3:-}\"\n65\t\n66\t  # Consume all of almanac_harden_role's output (no early awk exit) so the\n67\t  # producer never takes a SIGPIPE under `set -o pipefail`.\n68\t  almanac_harden_role \"$role\" \"$lens\" | awk -F'\\t' -v k=\"$field\" '$1 == k { v = $2 } END { print v }'\n69\t}\n70\t\n71\talmanac_harden_rubric_path() {\n72\t  local root=\"$1\"\n73\t  local target=\"$2\"\n74\t  local slug\n75\t\n76\t  slug=\"$(almanac_loop_slug \"$target\")\"\n77\t  printf '%s/docs/plans/harden/%s/rubric.md\\n' \"$root\" \"$slug\"\n78\t}\n79\t\n80\talmanac_harden_write_rubric() {\n81\t  local root=\"$1\"\n82\t  local target=\"$2\"\n83\t  local goal=\"$3\"\n84\t  local path dir\n85\t\n86\t  path=\"$(almanac_harden_rubric_path \"$root\" \"$target\")\"\n87\t  dir=\"$(dirname \"$path\")\"\n88\t\n89\t  if [ -e \"$path\" ]; then\n90\t    return 2\n91\t  fi\n92\t\n93\t  mkdir -p \"$dir\"\n94\t  cat > \"$path\" <<EOF\n95\t# Harden Rubric\n96\t\n97\tTarget: $target\n98\tStatus: draft\n99\t\n100\t## Goal\n101\t\n102\t$goal\n103\t\n104\t## Acceptance\n105\t\n106\t- [ ] Target behavior satisfies the stated goal.\n107\t- [ ] Blocking findings include a failing test, breaking input, or cited acceptance violation.\n108\t- [ ] Project feedback loops pass after fixes.\n109\t\n110\t## In Scope\n111\t\n112\t- $target\n113\t\n114\t## Out of Scope\n115\t\n116\t- Add non-goals here before running reviewers.\n117\t\n118\t## Severity\n119\t\n120\tBlocking findings must be falsifiable and reproducible against the current target.\n121\tSubjective or unreproducible findings are non-blocking notes.\n122\t\n123\t## Context\n124\t\n125\t- Add intentional decisions and false-positive preemptions here before running reviewers.\n126\tEOF\n127\t}\n128\t\n129\talmanac_harden_approve_rubric() {\n130\t  local root=\"$1\"\n131\t  local target=\"$2\"\n132\t  local path approved_at tmp\n133\t\n134\t  path=\"$(almanac_harden_rubric_path \"$root\" \"$target\")\"\n135\t\n136\t  if [ ! -f \"$path\" ]; then\n137\t    return 2\n138\t  fi\n139\t\n140\t  if grep -Eq '^Status: approved$' \"$path\"; then\n141\t    return 3\n142\t  fi\n143\t\n144\t  approved_at=\"$(date -u '+%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ')\"\n145\t  tmp=\"$(mktemp \"${path}.XXXXXX\")\"\n146\t\n147\t  if grep -Eq '^Status: draft$' \"$path\"; then\n148\t    awk -v approved_at=\"$approved_at\" '\n149\t      /^Status: draft$/ && !replaced {\n150\t        print \"Status: approved\"\n151\t        replaced = 1\n152\t        next\n153\t      }\n154\t      { print }\n155\t      END {\n156\t        print \"\"\n157\t        print \"## Approval\"\n158\t        print \"\"\n159\t        print \"Approved: \" approved_at\n160\t      }\n161\t    ' \"$path\" > \"$tmp\"\n162\t  else\n163\t    awk -v approved_at=\"$approved_at\" '\n164\t      /^Target: / && !inserted {\n165\t        print\n166\t        print \"Status: approved\"\n167\t        inserted = 1\n168\t        next\n169\t      }\n170\t      { print }\n171\t      END {\n172\t        if (!inserted) {\n173\t          print \"Status: approved\"\n174\t        }\n175\t        print \"\"\n176\t        print \"## Approval\"\n177\t        print \"\"\n178\t        print \"Approved: \" approved_at\n179\t      }\n180\t    ' \"$path\" > \"$tmp\"\n181\t  fi\n182\t\n183\t  mv \"$tmp\" \"$path\"\n184\t}\n185\t\n186\t# Return 0 when the rubric is approved (locked), non-zero otherwise — including\n187\t# when it is still a draft or the file is absent. Pure read; the loop gates on\n188\t# this so reviewers never run against a half-authored bar.\n189\talmanac_harden_rubric_approved() {\n190\t  local rubric_path=\"$1\"\n191\t\n192\t  [ -f \"$rubric_path\" ] || return 1\n193\t  grep -Eq '^Status: approved$' \"$rubric_path\"\n194\t}\n195\t\n196\t# Emit the rubric's acceptance criteria — the bar reviewers and ratification work\n197\t# against. Prints every bullet line under the `## Acceptance` heading up to the\n198\t# next `## ` section. Empty when the rubric or section is absent. Pure read.\n199\talmanac_harden_rubric_acceptance() {\n200\t  local path=\"$1\"\n201\t\n202\t  [ -f \"$path\" ] || return 0\n203\t\n204\t  awk '\n205\t    /^## Acceptance[[:space:]]*$/ { in_acc = 1; next }\n206\t    in_acc && /^## / { in_acc = 0 }\n207\t    in_acc && /^- / { print }\n208\t  ' \"$path\"\n209\t}\n210\t\n211\t# Append one acceptance criterion to the rubric's `## Acceptance` section. This is\n212\t# how a ratified finding grows the bar: monotonic (criteria are only added), visible\n213\t# (a clean diff), and append-only. The new `- [ ] <criterion>` lands at the end of\n214\t# the Acceptance block, before the next section. Idempotent: an identical criterion\n215\t# is never re-added (returns 1, writes nothing) so re-ratifying a reopened finding\n216\t# cannot duplicate it. Returns 2 when the rubric or its Acceptance section is absent.\n217\talmanac_harden_rubric_append_criterion() {\n218\t  local path=\"$1\"\n219\t  local criterion=\"$2\"\n220\t  local tmp\n221\t\n222\t  [ -f \"$path\" ] || return 2\n223\t  grep -q '^## Acceptance[[:space:]]*$' \"$path\" || return 2\n224\t\n225\t  if grep -Fxq -- \"- [ ] $criterion\" \"$path\" || \\\n226\t      grep -Fxq -- \"- [x] $criterion\" \"$path\"; then\n227\t    return 1\n228\t  fi\n229\t\n230\t  tmp=\"$(mktemp \"${path}.XXXXXX\")\"\n231\t  awk -v crit=\"$criterion\" '\n232\t    /^## Acceptance[[:space:]]*$/ { print; in_acc = 1; next }\n233\t    in_acc && /^## / {\n234\t      print \"- [ ] \" crit\n235\t      inserted = 1\n236\t      in_acc = 0\n237\t      for (i = 1; i <= nb; i++) print blanks[i]\n238\t      nb = 0\n239\t      print\n240\t      next\n241\t    }\n242\t    in_acc && /^[[:space:]]*$/ { nb++; blanks[nb] = $0; next }\n243\t    in_acc {\n244\t      for (i = 1; i <= nb; i++) print blanks[i]\n245\t      nb = 0\n246\t      print\n247\t      next\n248\t    }\n249\t    { print }\n250\t    END {\n251\t      if (in_acc && !inserted) {\n252\t        print \"- [ ] \" crit\n253\t        for (i = 1; i <= nb; i++) print blanks[i]\n254\t      }\n255\t    }\n256\t  ' \"$path\" > \"$tmp\"\n257\t  mv \"$tmp\" \"$path\"\n258\t}\n259\t\n260\t# --- Rubric immutability guard -------------------------------------------------\n261\t#\n262\t# The rubric is the contract, and during a run it is immutable to agents: the\n263\t# goalposts move only by a deliberate human act (the developer editing the file\n264\t# between runs / approving it) or the conductor's controlled append at\n265\t# ratification (almanac_harden_rubric_append_criterion — a visible, monotonic\n266\t# diff that runs OUTSIDE the reviewer/fixer phase). Reviewers run read-only and\n267\t# cannot write the rubric; the fixer (later slice) has write access and could.\n268\t# These two helpers bracket an agent phase — snapshot before, verify after — and\n269\t# revert any agent edit, so a stray agent write during a run cannot lower the bar.\n270\t\n271\t# Snapshot the rubric to a protected temp copy and echo the snapshot path so the\n272\t# caller can pass it to almanac_harden_rubric_verify. Returns 2 (echoes nothing)\n273\t# when no rubric exists — an ad-hoc bare run with no drafted contract has nothing\n274\t# to guard.\n275\talmanac_harden_rubric_snapshot() {\n276\t  local rubric_path=\"$1\"\n277\t  local snap\n278\t\n279\t  [ -f \"$rubric_path\" ] || return 2\n280\t\n281\t  snap=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/almanac-rubric-lock.XXXXXX\")\"\n282\t  cp \"$rubric_path\" \"$snap\"\n283\t  printf '%s\\n' \"$snap\"\n284\t}\n285\t\n286\t# Verify the rubric is byte-identical to its snapshot; if an agent modified it\n287\t# during the guarded phase, revert it and warn (the contract is immutable to\n288\t# agents). Discards the snapshot either way. Returns 1 when a modification was\n289\t# reverted, 0 when unchanged, 2 when the snapshot is missing.\n290\talmanac_harden_rubric_verify() {\n291\t  local rubric_path=\"$1\"\n292\t  local snap=\"$2\"\n293\t\n294\t  [ -n \"$snap\" ] && [ -f \"$snap\" ] || return 2\n295\t\n296\t  if ! cmp -s \"$rubric_path\" \"$snap\"; then\n297\t    cp \"$snap\" \"$rubric_path\"\n298\t    rm -f \"$snap\"\n299\t    _warn \"Rubric was modified during the run; reverted (contract is immutable to agents — amend it directly between runs).\"\n300\t    return 1\n301\t  fi\n302\t\n303\t  rm -f \"$snap\"\n304\t  return 0\n305\t}\n306\t\n307\t# Emit the configured reviewer lens set, one lens per line. Defaults to the five\n308\t# PRD lenses; override at runtime via HARDEN_LENSES (comma- or whitespace-\n309\t# separated).\n310\talmanac_harden_lenses() {\n311\t  local raw=\"${HARDEN_LENSES:-correctness security perf edge-cases contracts}\"\n312\t\n313\t  # Trailing newline matters: a `read` loop consumer drops a final line that\n314\t  # lacks one, which would silently swallow the last lens.\n315\t  printf '%s\\n' \"$raw\" | tr -s ', \\t' '\\n' | sed '/^$/d'\n316\t}\n317\t\n318\talmanac_harden_max_reviewers() {\n319\t  printf '%s\\n' \"${HARDEN_MAX_REVIEWERS:-16}\"\n320\t}\n321\t\n322\t# Build the fixed prompt for one read-only reviewer over a target, including the\n323\t# JSON-Lines findings schema. When a rubric path is given and exists, the rubric's\n324\t# acceptance criteria are embedded as the bar the reviewer judges against, so\n325\t# reviewers consume the contract rather than an implicit standard. An optional\n326\t# steering directive (4th arg) is embedded too, so an operator who redirects the\n327\t# run at the HITL checkpoint (e.g. \"focus on the auth module\") reaches the\n328\t# reviewers on the next round. Kept separate so the schema can grow without\n329\t# touching orchestration. (Exact prompt wording is not asserted in tests by\n330\t# design; that the rubric bar and the steer directive are consumed is.)\n331\talmanac_harden_reviewer_prompt() {\n332\t  local target=\"$1\"\n333\t  local lens=\"${2:-correctness}\"\n334\t  local rubric_path=\"${3:-}\"\n335\t  local directive=\"${4:-}\"\n336\t  local rubric_bar=\"\"\n337\t\n338\t  if [ -n \"$rubric_path\" ] && [ -f \"$rubric_path\" ]; then\n339\t    rubric_bar=\"$(almanac_harden_rubric_acceptance \"$rubric_path\")\"\n340\t  fi\n341\t\n342\t  cat <<EOF\n343\tYou are a read-only code reviewer. Lens: ${lens}.\n344\t\n345\tReview the target below for ${lens} defects only. You cannot modify any files;\n346\tthis is a read-only review.\n347\t\n348\tTarget: ${target}\n349\tEOF\n350\t\n351\t  if [ -n \"$rubric_bar\" ]; then\n352\t    cat <<EOF\n353\t\n354\tJudge the target against this acceptance bar (the rubric contract). A finding is\n355\tonly blocking if it violates a criterion below or demonstrably breaks behavior:\n356\t\n357\t${rubric_bar}\n358\tEOF\n359\t  fi\n360\t\n361\t  if [ -n \"$directive\" ]; then\n362\t    cat <<EOF\n363\t\n364\tThe operator steered this run with the directive below — follow it and prioritize\n365\tthe findings it points you toward:\n366\t\n367\t${directive}\n368\tEOF\n369\t  fi\n370\t\n371\t  cat <<EOF\n372\t\n373\tReport each defect as one JSON object per line (JSON Lines) and output nothing\n374\telse — no prose, no markdown fences. Each object must use this schema:\n375\t\n376\t{\"lens\":\"${lens}\",\"severity\":\"high|medium|low\",\"location\":\"<file:line or symbol>\",\"claim\":\"<one-line defect>\",\"demonstration\":\"<failing test, breaking input, or cited rubric criterion>\"}\n377\t\n378\tOnly report a defect you can demonstrate with a failing test, a specific breaking\n379\tinput, or a cited criterion. If you find no demonstrable defects, output nothing.\n380\tEOF\n381\t}\n382\t\n383\t# Normalize the reviewer's JSON-Lines result into TSV rows\n384\t# (lens, severity, location, claim, demonstration). Malformed lines are dropped\n385\t# cleanly. Prefers jq; falls back to a flat-field awk extractor when jq is absent\n386\t# so harden keeps almanac's near-zero-dependency promise.\n387\talmanac_harden_findings_tsv() {\n388\t  local result_file=\"$1\"\n389\t\n390\t  [ -f \"$result_file\" ] || return 0\n391\t\n392\t  if command -v jq >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n393\t    jq -Rr '\n394\t      fromjson?\n395\t      | select(type == \"object\")\n396\t      | {\n397\t          lens: (.lens // \"\"),\n398\t          severity: (.severity // \"\"),\n399\t          location: (.location // \"\"),\n400\t          claim: (.claim // \"\"),\n401\t          demonstration: (.demonstration // \"\")\n402\t        }\n403\t      | select(\n404\t          (.lens | type == \"string\" and length > 0) and\n405\t          (.severity | type == \"string\" and length > 0) and\n406\t          (.location | type == \"string\" and length > 0) and\n407\t          (.claim | type == \"string\" and length > 0) and\n408\t          (.demonstration | type == \"string\" and length > 0)\n409\t        )\n410\t      | [.lens, .severity, .location, .claim, .demonstration]\n411\t      | @tsv\n412\t    ' \"$result_file\" 2>/dev/null\n413\t    return 0\n414\t  fi\n415\t\n416\t  awk '\n417\t    function field(line, key,   v) {\n418\t      v = line\n419\t      if (v ~ (\"\\\"\" key \"\\\"[ \\t]*:[ \\t]*\\\"\")) {\n420\t        sub(\".*\\\"\" key \"\\\"[ \\t]*:[ \\t]*\\\"\", \"\", v)\n421\t        sub(\"\\\".*\", \"\", v)\n422\t        return v\n423\t      }\n424\t      return \"\"\n425\t    }\n426\t    /\"claim\"[ \\t]*:/ {\n427\t      lens = field($0, \"lens\")\n428\t      severity = field($0, \"severity\")\n429\t      location = field($0, \"location\")\n430\t      claim = field($0, \"claim\")\n431\t      demonstration = field($0, \"demonstration\")\n432\t      if (lens != \"\" && severity != \"\" && location != \"\" && claim != \"\" && demonstration != \"\") {\n433\t        printf \"%s\\t%s\\t%s\\t%s\\t%s\\n\", lens, severity, location, claim, demonstration\n434\t      }\n435\t    }\n436\t  ' \"$result_file\"\n437\t}\n438\t\n439\t# Print parsed findings as a readable list. Reports \"No findings reported.\" when\n440\t# the reviewer returned nothing parseable.\n441\talmanac_harden_format_findings() {\n442\t  local result_file=\"$1\"\n443\t  local lens severity location claim demonstration count\n444\t\n445\t  count=0\n446\t  while IFS=$'\\t' read -r lens severity location claim demonstration; do\n447\t    [ -n \"${lens}${severity}${location}${claim}${demonstration}\" ] || continue\n448\t    printf -- '- [%s] %s: %s\\n' \"${severity:-?}\" \"${lens:-?}\" \"${claim:-?}\"\n449\t    [ -n \"$location\" ] && printf '    where: %s\\n' \"$location\"\n450\t    [ -n \"$demonstration\" ] && printf '    demo:  %s\\n' \"$demonstration\"\n451\t    count=$((count + 1))\n452\t  done < <(almanac_harden_findings_tsv \"$result_file\")\n453\t\n454\t  if [ \"$count\" -eq 0 ]; then\n455\t    printf '%s\\n' \"No findings reported.\"\n456\t  fi\n457\t}\n458\t\n459\t# --- Findings ledger -----------------------------------------------------------\n460\t#\n461\t# Canonical finding schema (one JSON object per reviewer line, see the reviewer\n462\t# prompt above): lens, severity, location, claim, demonstration. The ledger adds\n463\t# three adjudication fields when a finding is recorded:\n464\t#   id            - deterministic fingerprint of (lens, location, claim)\n465\t#   status        - open | fixed | rejected-subjective | wontfix-per-context\n466\t#   round         - the review round that first raised the finding\n467\t#   adjudication  - free-text note (why rejected / how fixed); empty when open\n468\t#\n469\t# Findings persist append-only to findings.md next to the target's rubric.md.\n470\t# Each finding is one markdown section keyed by its id, so the file is both\n471\t# human-readable and re-parseable (dedupe + open-blocking query read it back).\n472\t\n473\talmanac_harden_ledger_path() {\n474\t  local root=\"$1\"\n475\t  local target=\"$2\"\n476\t  local slug\n477\t\n478\t  slug=\"$(almanac_loop_slug \"$target\")\"\n479\t  printf '%s/docs/plans/harden/%s/findings.md\\n' \"$root\" \"$slug\"\n480\t}\n481\t\n482\t# Deterministic finding identity. Two reviewer reports of the same defect\n483\t# (same lens, same place, same claim) collapse to one id so re-raising a\n484\t# finding never re-adds it. Demonstration is deliberately excluded: a reworded\n485\t# repro must not look like a new finding. cksum keeps this dependency-free.\n486\talmanac_harden_finding_id() {\n487\t  local lens=\"$1\"\n488\t  local location=\"$2\"\n489\t  local claim=\"$3\"\n490\t  local sum\n491\t\n492\t  sum=\"$(printf '%s\\037%s\\037%s' \"$lens\" \"$location\" \"$claim\" | cksum | awk '{print $1}')\"\n493\t  printf 'f-%s\\n' \"$sum\"\n494\t}\n495\t\n496\talmanac_harden_ledger_init() {\n497\t  local path=\"$1\"\n498\t  local dir\n499\t\n500\t  dir=\"$(dirname \"$path\")\"\n501\t  mkdir -p \"$dir\"\n502\t\n503\t  if [ ! -f \"$path\" ]; then\n504\t    {\n505\t      printf '%s\\n\\n' \"# Findings Ledger\"\n506\t      printf '%s\\n' \"<!-- Append-only finding records managed by 'almanac harden'. One section per finding. -->\"\n507\t    } > \"$path\"\n508\t  fi\n509\t}\n510\t\n511\t# True when the ledger already holds a finding with this id.\n512\talmanac_harden_ledger_has() {\n513\t  local path=\"$1\"\n514\t  local id=\"$2\"\n515\t\n516\t  [ -f \"$path\" ] || return 1\n517\t  grep -Fxq -- \"## $id\" \"$path\"\n518\t}\n519\t\n520\t# Append one finding section. Returns 1 (and writes nothing) when the id is\n521\t# already present, so callers can count genuinely-new findings. Creates the\n522\t# ledger file with its header on first write.\n523\talmanac_harden_ledger_append_entry() {\n524\t  [ \"$#\" -ge 7 ] || return 2\n525\t\n526\t  local path=\"$1\"\n527\t  local id=\"$2\"\n528\t  local lens=\"$3\"\n529\t  local severity=\"$4\"\n530\t  local location=\"$5\"\n531\t  local claim=\"$6\"\n532\t  local demonstration=\"$7\"\n533\t  local status=\"${8:-open}\"\n534\t  local round=\"${9:-1}\"\n535\t  local adjudication=\"${10:-}\"\n536\t\n537\t  almanac_harden_ledger_init \"$path\"\n538\t\n539\t  if almanac_harden_ledger_has \"$path\" \"$id\"; then\n540\t    return 1\n541\t  fi\n542\t\n543\t  almanac_harden_ledger_append_entry_unchecked \\\n544\t    \"$path\" \"$id\" \"$lens\" \"$severity\" \"$location\" \"$claim\" \\\n545\t    \"$demonstration\" \"$status\" \"$round\" \"$adjudication\"\n546\t}\n547\t\n548\t# Append one already-deduped finding section. Callers must have initialised the\n549\t# ledger and decided the id is new; this keeps bulk ingestion from grepping the\n550\t# growing ledger once per finding.\n551\talmanac_harden_ledger_append_entry_unchecked() {\n552\t  [ \"$#\" -ge 7 ] || return 2\n553\t\n554\t  local path=\"$1\"\n555\t  local id=\"$2\"\n556\t  local lens=\"$3\"\n557\t  local severity=\"$4\"\n558\t  local location=\"$5\"\n559\t  local claim=\"$6\"\n560\t  local demonstration=\"$7\"\n561\t  local status=\"${8:-open}\"\n562\t  local round=\"${9:-1}\"\n563\t  local adjudication=\"${10:-}\"\n564\t\n565\t  {\n566\t    printf '\\n## %s\\n\\n' \"$id\"\n567\t    printf -- '- lens: %s\\n' \"$lens\"\n568\t    printf -- '- severity: %s\\n' \"$severity\"\n569\t    printf -- '- location: %s\\n' \"$location\"\n570\t    printf -- '- claim: %s\\n' \"$claim\"\n571\t    printf -- '- demonstration: %s\\n' \"$demonstration\"\n572\t    printf -- '- status: %s\\n' \"$status\"\n573\t    printf -- '- round: %s\\n' \"$round\"\n574\t    printf -- '- adjudication: %s\\n' \"$adjudication\"\n575\t  } >> \"$path\"\n576\t}\n577\t\n578\t# Normalize a reviewer's JSON-Lines result into ledger-entry TSV rows\n579\t# (id, lens, severity, location, claim, demonstration, status, round,\n580\t# adjudication). New findings are status=open with an empty adjudication.\n581\t# Malformed reviewer lines are dropped cleanly (via almanac_harden_findings_tsv).\n582\talmanac_harden_parse_findings() {\n583\t  local result_file=\"$1\"\n584\t  local round=\"${2:-1}\"\n585\t  local lens severity location claim demonstration id\n586\t\n587\t  while IFS=$'\\t' read -r lens severity location claim demonstration; do\n588\t    [ -n \"${lens}${severity}${location}${claim}${demonstration}\" ] || continue\n589\t    id=\"$(almanac_harden_finding_id \"$lens\" \"$location\" \"$claim\")\"\n590\t    printf '%s\\t%s\\t%s\\t%s\\t%s\\t%s\\t%s\\t%s\\t%s\\n' \\\n591\t      \"$id\" \"$lens\" \"$severity\" \"$location\" \"$claim\" \"$demonstration\" \"open\" \"$round\" \"\"\n592\t  done < <(almanac_harden_findings_tsv \"$result_file\")\n593\t}\n594\t\n595\t# Parse a reviewer result and append each new finding to the ledger, deduping\n596\t# against everything already adjudicated. Prints the count of findings actually\n597\t# added (duplicates do not count).\n598\talmanac_harden_ledger_record() {\n599\t  local path=\"$1\"\n600\t  local result_file=\"$2\"\n601\t  local round=\"${3:-1}\"\n602\t  local parsed statuses actions reopen_ids action\n603\t  local id lens severity location claim demonstration status r adjudication\n604\t  local added=0\n605\t\n606\t  almanac_harden_ledger_init \"$path\"\n607\t\n608\t  parsed=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/almanac-harden-findings.XXXXXX\")\"\n609\t  statuses=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/almanac-harden-statuses.XXXXXX\")\"\n610\t  actions=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/almanac-harden-actions.XXXXXX\")\"\n611\t  reopen_ids=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/almanac-harden-reopen.XXXXXX\")\"\n612\t\n613\t  almanac_harden_parse_findings \"$result_file\" \"$round\" > \"$parsed\"\n614\t\n615\t  awk '\n616\t    /^## / { id = substr($0, 4); next }\n617\t    /^- status:/ && id != \"\" {\n618\t      val = $0\n619\t      sub(/^- status:[ \\t]*/, \"\", val)\n620\t      print id \"\\t\" val\n621\t    }\n622\t  ' \"$path\" > \"$statuses\"\n623\t\n624\t  awk '\n625\t    BEGIN { FS = \"\\t\" }\n626\t    FILENAME == ARGV[1] { existing[$1] = $2; next }\n627\t    $1 == \"\" { next }\n628\t    seen[$1]++ { next }\n629\t    !($1 in existing) {\n630\t      print \"append\\t\" $0\n631\t      next\n632\t    }\n633\t    existing[$1] == \"fixed\" {\n634\t      print \"reopen\\t\" $0\n635\t      next\n636\t    }\n637\t  ' \"$statuses\" \"$parsed\" > \"$actions\"\n638\t\n639\t  while IFS=$'\\t' read -r action id lens severity location claim demonstration status r adjudication; do\n640\t    [ -n \"$id\" ] || continue\n641\t    case \"$action\" in\n642\t      append)\n643\t        almanac_harden_ledger_append_entry_unchecked \\\n644\t          \"$path\" \"$id\" \"$lens\" \"$severity\" \"$location\" \"$claim\" \\\n645\t          \"$demonstration\" \"$status\" \"$r\" \"$adjudication\"\n646\t        added=$((added + 1))\n647\t        ;;\n648\t      reopen)\n649\t        printf '%s\\n' \"$id\" >> \"$reopen_ids\"\n650\t        ;;\n651\t    esac\n652\t  done < \"$actions\"\n653\t\n654\t  if [ -s \"$reopen_ids\" ]; then\n655\t    almanac_harden_ledger_set_status_many \"$path\" \"open\" \\\n656\t      \"re-raised by reviewer at round $round; pending ratification\" < \"$reopen_ids\"\n657\t  fi\n658\t\n659\t  rm -f \"$parsed\" \"$statuses\" \"$actions\" \"$reopen_ids\"\n660\t\n661\t  printf '%s\\n' \"$added\"\n662\t}\n663\t\n664\t# Emit the open blocking findings as TSV rows\n665\t# (id, lens, severity, location, claim, demonstration). Only status=open\n666\t# entries qualify; fixed / rejected-subjective / wontfix-per-context never gate.\n667\talmanac_harden_ledger_open_blocking() {\n668\t  local path=\"$1\"\n669\t\n670\t  [ -f \"$path\" ] || return 0\n671\t\n672\t  awk '\n673\t    function flush() {\n674\t      if (id != \"\" && status == \"open\") {\n675\t        printf \"%s\\t%s\\t%s\\t%s\\t%s\\t%s\\n\", id, lens, severity, location, claim, demonstration\n676\t      }\n677\t    }\n678\t    /^## / {\n679\t      flush()\n680\t      id = substr($0, 4)\n681\t      lens = \"\"; severity = \"\"; location = \"\"; claim = \"\"; demonstration = \"\"; status = \"\"\n682\t      next\n683\t    }\n684\t    /^- / {\n685\t      line = substr($0, 3)\n686\t      p = index(line, \":\")\n687\t      if (p == 0) next\n688\t      key = substr(line, 1, p - 1)\n689\t      val = substr(line, p + 1)\n690\t      sub(/^ /, \"\", val)\n691\t      if (key == \"lens\") lens = val\n692\t      else if (key == \"severity\") severity = val\n693\t      else if (key == \"location\") location = val\n694\t      else if (key == \"claim\") claim = val\n695\t      else if (key == \"demonstration\") demonstration = val\n696\t      else if (key == \"status\") status = val\n697\t    }\n698\t    END { flush() }\n699\t  ' \"$path\"\n700\t}\n701\t\n702\t# Print the recorded status of the finding with this id (empty when the id is\n703\t# not in the ledger). Used by ratification to tell new from already-adjudicated.\n704\talmanac_harden_ledger_status() {\n705\t  local path=\"$1\"\n706\t  local id=\"$2\"\n707\t\n708\t  [ -f \"$path\" ] || return 0\n709\t\n710\t  awk -v want=\"$id\" '\n711\t    /^## / { cur = substr($0, 4); next }\n712\t    /^- status:/ && cur == want {\n713\t      val = $0\n714\t      sub(/^- status:[ \\t]*/, \"\", val)\n715\t      print val\n716\t      exit\n717\t    }\n718\t  ' \"$path\"\n719\t}\n720\t\n721\t# Rewrite the status (and adjudication note) of the finding with this id in\n722\t# place, leaving every other field and finding untouched. Returns 1 when the\n723\t# ledger file is absent.\n724\talmanac_harden_ledger_set_status() {\n725\t  local path=\"$1\"\n726\t  local id=\"$2\"\n727\t  local status=\"$3\"\n728\t  local adjudication=\"${4:-}\"\n729\t  local tmp\n730\t\n731\t  [ -f \"$path\" ] || return 1\n732\t\n733\t  tmp=\"$(mktemp \"${path}.XXXXXX\")\"\n734\t  awk -v want=\"$id\" -v status=\"$status\" -v adj=\"$adjudication\" '\n735\t    /^## / { cur = substr($0, 4); print; next }\n736\t    cur == want && /^- status:/ { print \"- status: \" status; next }\n737\t    cur == want && /^- adjudication:/ { print \"- adjudication: \" adj; next }\n738\t    { print }\n739\t  ' \"$path\" > \"$tmp\"\n740\t  mv \"$tmp\" \"$path\"\n741\t}\n742\t\n743\t# Rewrite status/adjudication for many finding ids in one ledger pass. Reads ids\n744\t# from stdin, one per line. Used after a batch fix so marking N findings fixed is\n745\t# O(ledger) instead of N full ledger rewrites.\n746\talmanac_harden_ledger_set_status_many() {\n747\t  local path=\"$1\"\n748\t  local status=\"$2\"\n749\t  local adjudication=\"${3:-}\"\n750\t  local ids tmp\n751\t\n752\t  [ -f \"$path\" ] || return 1\n753\t\n754\t  ids=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/almanac-harden-ids.XXXXXX\")\"\n755\t  cat > \"$ids\"\n756\t  [ -s \"$ids\" ] || { rm -f \"$ids\"; return 0; }\n757\t\n758\t  tmp=\"$(mktemp \"${path}.XXXXXX\")\"\n759\t  awk -v ids=\"$ids\" -v status=\"$status\" -v adj=\"$adjudication\" '\n760\t    BEGIN {\n761\t      while ((getline line < ids) > 0) {\n762\t        if (line != \"\") wanted[line] = 1\n763\t      }\n764\t      close(ids)\n765\t    }\n766\t    /^## / { cur = substr($0, 4); print; next }\n767\t    (cur in wanted) && /^- status:/ { print \"- status: \" status; next }\n768\t    (cur in wanted) && /^- adjudication:/ { print \"- adjudication: \" adj; next }\n769\t    { print }\n770\t  ' \"$path\" > \"$tmp\"\n771\t  mv \"$tmp\" \"$path\"\n772\t  rm -f \"$ids\"\n773\t}\n774\t\n775\t# --- Ratification engine -------------------------------------------------------\n776\t#\n777\t# A finding is \"blocking\" only if its demonstration objectively reproduces\n778\t# against the current target — never on a reviewer's assertion alone. Execution\n779\t# of the demonstration is isolated behind a seam (almanac_harden_demo_reproduces)\n780\t# so the decision logic is testable without running anything, and so the real\n781\t# executor (a conductor agent-runner call) can be wired in a later slice.\n782\t\n783\t# Prompt the conductor uses to execute one finding's demonstration. It must run\n784\t# the demonstration against the CURRENT code and render a strict, falsifiable\n785\t# verdict — never an opinion. The verdict contract is a single machine-readable\n786\t# token so the parser can be unambiguous (see almanac_harden_ratify_verdict).\n787\talmanac_harden_ratify_prompt() {\n788\t  local demonstration=\"$1\"\n789\t  local target_path=\"${2:-}\"\n790\t\n791\t  cat <<EOF\n792\tYou are the CONDUCTOR in a code-hardening loop. Ratify ONE reviewer finding by\n793\tEXECUTING its demonstration against the current code — decide by reproduction,\n794\tnever by opinion.\n795\t\n796\tTarget: ${target_path:-(the current working directory)}\n797\t\n798\tDemonstration to reproduce:\n799\t${demonstration}\n800\t\n801\tDo this:\n802\t1. Carry out the demonstration against the code AS IT IS RIGHT NOW: run the\n803\t   proposed failing test, try the specific breaking input, or check the cited\n804\t   rubric criterion.\n805\t2. Decide strictly. The finding reproduces ONLY if the defect actually manifests\n806\t   against the current code. A demonstration that you cannot run, that is vague\n807\t   or speculative, or that does not actually fail does NOT reproduce.\n808\t3. You are a JUDGE, not a fixer: do not modify the target to change the outcome.\n809\t\n810\tEnd your message with EXACTLY ONE of these two lines and nothing after it:\n811\tHARDEN_VERDICT=reproduces\n812\tHARDEN_VERDICT=not-reproduces\n813\tEOF\n814\t}\n815\t\n816\t# Parse the conductor's final message into a reproduce verdict. The contract is a\n817\t# single unambiguous token: the affirmative is the literal \"HARDEN_VERDICT=reproduces\"\n818\t# (the negative \"HARDEN_VERDICT=not-reproduces\" cannot match it — the char after\n819\t# `=` is `n`, not `r`). Anything else (no token, garbled, only the negative) reads\n820\t# as \"not\", so an un-parseable verdict is conservatively a non-blocking note.\n821\talmanac_harden_ratify_verdict() {\n822\t  local result_file=\"$1\"\n823\t\n824\t  [ -f \"$result_file\" ] || { printf '%s\\n' \"not\"; return 0; }\n825\t\n826\t  if grep -Fxq 'HARDEN_VERDICT=reproduces' \"$result_file\" 2>/dev/null; then\n827\t    printf '%s\\n' \"reproduces\"\n828\t  else\n829\t    printf '%s\\n' \"not\"\n830\t  fi\n831\t}\n832\t\n833\t# Execution seam: decide whether a finding's demonstration reproduces against the\n834\t# target. Return 0 = reproduces (real defect, blocking), non-zero = does not\n835\t# reproduce (opinion / stale). This seam IS the conductor executing the\n836\t# demonstration: it runs the demonstration through the resolved conductor provider\n837\t# (the (provider, model, effort) it is handed — no host-marker dependence, so it\n838\t# is mixable per the role config) via the shared agent runner and reads the\n839\t# conductor's verdict back from its final message. PRD story 8: \"blocking means\n840\t# objectively reproducible, not a reviewer's assertion.\"\n841\t#\n842\t# Conservative on every uncertainty so opinions never silently gate the loop and\n843\t# a flaky/missing provider never blocks a run: an empty demonstration, an\n844\t# unresolved conductor provider, a failed/un-runnable conductor call, or an\n845\t# un-parseable verdict all read as non-reproducing (a note). Tests override this\n846\t# to drive the decision paths directly; here it is the real executor.\n847\talmanac_harden_demo_reproduces() {\n848\t  local demonstration=\"$1\"\n849\t  local target_path=\"${2:-}\"\n850\t  local conductor_provider=\"${3:-}\"\n851\t  local conductor_model=\"${4:-}\"\n852\t  local conductor_effort=\"${5:-}\"\n853\t  local prompt_file result_file events_file verdict rc\n854\t\n855\t  # Nothing to execute / no provider to execute it through -> conservative note.\n856\t  [ -n \"$demonstration\" ] || return 1\n857\t  [ -n \"$conductor_provider\" ] || return 1\n858\t\n859\t  prompt_file=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/almanac-harden-ratify-prompt.XXXXXX\")\" || return 1\n860\t  result_file=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/almanac-harden-ratify-result.XXXXXX\")\" || { rm -f \"$prompt_file\"; return 1; }\n861\t  events_file=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/almanac-harden-ratify-events.XXXXXX\")\" || { rm -f \"$prompt_file\" \"$result_file\"; return 1; }\n862\t\n863\t  almanac_harden_ratify_prompt \"$demonstration\" \"$target_path\" > \"$prompt_file\"\n864\t\n865\t  # Reviewer text is untrusted. Ratification may inspect/run existing repro\n866\t  # commands, but it must not write to the repo before the single fixer phase.\n867\t  rc=0\n868\t  almanac_loop_agent_capture \"$conductor_provider\" \"$conductor_model\" \"$conductor_effort\" \\\n869\t    \"read-only\" \"$prompt_file\" \"$result_file\" \"$events_file\" >/dev/null 2>&1 || rc=$?\n870\t\n871\t  if [ \"$rc\" -ne 0 ]; then\n872\t    # Provider missing/crashed or the demonstration was un-runnable: cannot\n873\t    # confirm reproduction -> non-blocking note, never a hang or a hard failure.\n874\t    rm -f \"$prompt_file\" \"$result_file\" \"$events_file\"\n875\t    return 1\n876\t  fi\n877\t\n878\t  verdict=\"$(almanac_harden_ratify_verdict \"$result_file\")\"\n879\t  rm -f \"$prompt_file\" \"$result_file\" \"$events_file\"\n880\t\n881\t  [ \"$verdict\" = \"reproduces\" ] && return 0\n882\t  return 1\n883\t}\n884\t\n885\t# Adjudicate one finding by executing its demonstration through the seam and\n886\t# recording the outcome in the ledger. Prints the verdict:\n887\t#   blocking - new/open finding whose demonstration reproduces (ratified, gates)\n888\t#   note     - new/open finding that does not reproduce (non-blocking note)\n889\t#   reopened - an already-adjudicated finding whose demonstration newly reproduces\n890\t#   dropped  - an already-adjudicated finding that still does not reproduce\n891\t# Already-adjudicated findings are re-litigated ONLY when they newly reproduce,\n892\t# so a rejected opinion cannot churn the loop round after round.\n893\t#\n894\t# When a rubric path is given, a finding that reproduces (blocking or reopened)\n895\t# also appends a falsifiable criterion to the rubric's `## Acceptance` — the bar\n896\t# grows monotonically and visibly with every ratified defect. Notes and drops\n897\t# never touch the rubric, so opinions cannot raise the bar.\n898\t#\n899\t# The trailing conductor (provider, model, effort) args (11th-13th) identify the\n900\t# provider that executes the demonstration; they are passed straight to the\n901\t# execution seam. Optional/backward-compatible — omit them to use the default.\n902\talmanac_harden_ratify() {\n903\t  local path=\"$1\"\n904\t  local id=\"$2\"\n905\t  local lens=\"$3\"\n906\t  local severity=\"$4\"\n907\t  local location=\"$5\"\n908\t  local claim=\"$6\"\n909\t  local demonstration=\"$7\"\n910\t  local round=\"${8:-1}\"\n911\t  local target_path=\"${9:-}\"\n912\t  local rubric_path=\"${10:-}\"\n913\t  local conductor_provider=\"${11:-}\"\n914\t  local conductor_model=\"${12:-}\"\n915\t  local conductor_effort=\"${13:-}\"\n916\t  local current_status reproduces status note\n917\t\n918\t  almanac_harden_ledger_init \"$path\"\n919\t  current_status=\"$(almanac_harden_ledger_status \"$path\" \"$id\")\"\n920\t\n921\t  if almanac_harden_demo_reproduces \"$demonstration\" \"$target_path\" \\\n922\t      \"$conductor_provider\" \"$conductor_model\" \"$conductor_effort\"; then\n923\t    reproduces=1\n924\t  else\n925\t    reproduces=0\n926\t  fi\n927\t\n928\t  # A ratified (reproducing) finding grows the rubric bar, regardless of whether\n929\t  # it is newly raised or a reopened prior finding. Idempotent on the criterion\n930\t  # text, so a reopen never duplicates an already-listed criterion.\n931\t  if [ \"$reproduces\" -eq 1 ] && [ -n \"$rubric_path\" ]; then\n932\t    almanac_harden_rubric_append_criterion \"$rubric_path\" \\\n933\t      \"${claim} — must not reproduce (lens: ${lens}, at ${location})\" >/dev/null || true\n934\t  fi\n935\t\n936\t  case \"$current_status\" in\n937\t    fixed | rejected-subjective | wontfix-per-context)\n938\t      if [ \"$reproduces\" -eq 1 ]; then\n939\t        almanac_harden_ledger_set_status \"$path\" \"$id\" \"open\" \\\n940\t          \"reopened: demonstration reproduced at round $round\"\n941\t        printf '%s\\n' \"reopened\"\n942\t      else\n943\t        printf '%s\\n' \"dropped\"\n944\t      fi\n945\t      return 0\n946\t      ;;\n947\t  esac\n948\t\n949\t  if [ \"$reproduces\" -eq 1 ]; then\n950\t    status=\"open\"\n951\t    note=\"ratified: demonstration reproduced at round $round\"\n952\t  else\n953\t    status=\"rejected-subjective\"\n954\t    note=\"did not reproduce at round $round\"\n955\t  fi\n956\t\n957\t  if [ -z \"$current_status\" ]; then\n958\t    almanac_harden_ledger_append_entry \"$path\" \"$id\" \"$lens\" \"$severity\" \\\n959\t      \"$location\" \"$claim\" \"$demonstration\" \"$status\" \"$round\" \"$note\" >/dev/null\n960\t  else\n961\t    almanac_harden_ledger_set_status \"$path\" \"$id\" \"$status\" \"$note\"\n962\t  fi\n963\t\n964\t  if [ \"$reproduces\" -eq 1 ]; then\n965\t    printf '%s\\n' \"blocking\"\n966\t  else\n967\t    printf '%s\\n' \"note\"\n968\t  fi\n969\t}\n970\t\n971\t# Fan out one read-only reviewer per configured lens as a background worker via\n972\t# the shared worker orchestration, then aggregate every reviewer's findings into\n973\t# the ledger (deduped). Reviewers run concurrently and never write to the target\n974\t# (read-only sandbox); the parent aggregates sequentially after they finish, so\n975\t# there are no concurrent ledger writers. The lens set is configurable via\n976\t# HARDEN_LENSES, capped by HARDEN_MAX_REVIEWERS. Each reviewer's\n977\t# provider/model/effort resolves through the shared role config\n978\t# (HARDEN_REVIEWER[_<LENS>]_{PROVIDER,MODEL,EFFORT}). _die on a missing target\n979\t# before spawning anything.\n980\talmanac_harden_fanout() {\n981\t  local root=\"$1\"\n982\t  local target=\"$2\"\n983\t  local round=\"${3:-1}\"\n984\t  local directive=\"${4:-}\"\n985\t  local target_path run_id run_id_base registry_dir ledger_path rubric_path lens provider model effort\n986\t  local worker_id prompt_file pidfile pid result_file status_file wstatus\n987\t  local added total_added i max_reviewers succeeded_count suffix\n988\t  local -a lenses=() worker_ids=() worker_pids=() prompt_files=()\n989\t\n990\t  case \"$target\" in\n991\t    /*) target_path=\"$target\" ;;\n992\t    *)  target_path=\"$root/$target\" ;;\n993\t  esac\n994\t\n995\t  if [ ! -e \"$target_path\" ]; then\n996\t    _die \"Harden target not found: $target\"\n997\t  fi\n998\t\n999\t  while IFS= read -r lens; do\n1000\t    [ -n \"$lens\" ] || continue\n1001\t    lenses+=(\"$lens\")\n1002\t  done < <(almanac_harden_lenses)\n1003\t\n1004\t  [ \"${#lenses[@]}\" -gt 0 ] || _die \"No reviewer lenses configured\"\n1005\t  max_reviewers=\"$(almanac_harden_max_reviewers)\"\n1006\t  case \"$max_reviewers\" in\n1007\t    ''|*[!0-9]*) _die \"HARDEN_MAX_REVIEWERS must be a positive integer: $max_reviewers\" ;;\n1008\t  esac\n1009\t  [ \"$max_reviewers\" -ge 1 ] || _die \"HARDEN_MAX_REVIEWERS must be at least 1: $max_reviewers\"\n1010\t  if [ \"${#lenses[@]}\" -gt \"$max_reviewers\" ]; then\n1011\t    _die \"Too many reviewer lenses (${#lenses[@]}); cap is $max_reviewers (set HARDEN_MAX_REVIEWERS to change it)\"\n1012\t  fi\n1013\t\n1014\t  run_id=\"$(almanac_loop_run_id \"harden\" \"$target\")\"\n1015\t  run_id_base=\"$run_id\"\n1016\t  registry_dir=\"$(almanac_loop_registry_dir \"$root\")\"\n1017\t  suffix=1\n1018\t  while [ -e \"$registry_dir/$run_id\" ]; do\n1019\t    suffix=$((suffix + 1))\n1020\t    run_id=\"${run_id_base}-${suffix}\"\n1021\t  done\n1022\t  ledger_path=\"$(almanac_harden_ledger_path \"$root\" \"$target\")\"\n1023\t  rubric_path=\"$(almanac_harden_rubric_path \"$root\" \"$target\")\"\n1024\t\n1025\t  # The rubric is the contract; once one has been drafted it must be approved\n1026\t  # (locked) before the loop proceeds, so reviewers never run against a bar the\n1027\t  # human is still authoring. No rubric at all = an explicit ad-hoc run; proceed.\n1028\t  if [ -f \"$rubric_path\" ] && ! almanac_harden_rubric_approved \"$rubric_path\"; then\n1029\t    _die \"Rubric not approved: ${rubric_path#\"$root\"/} — edit it, then: almanac harden $target --approve\"\n1030\t  fi\n1031\t\n1032\t  almanac_harden_ledger_init \"$ledger_path\"\n1033\t\n1034\t  # The rubric is immutable to agents during the run. Snapshot it before any\n1035\t  # reviewer spawns; the reviewer round makes no legitimate rubric edits (the\n1036\t  # conductor's controlled append happens at ratification, a later phase), so\n1037\t  # any change observed when reviewers finish is an agent tampering — revert it.\n1038\t  local rubric_snapshot=\"\"\n1039\t  if [ -f \"$rubric_path\" ]; then\n1040\t    rubric_snapshot=\"$(almanac_harden_rubric_snapshot \"$rubric_path\")\" || rubric_snapshot=\"\"\n1041\t  fi\n1042\t\n1043\t  _info \"Hardening $target — fanning out ${#lenses[@]} read-only reviewer(s)\"\n1044\t\n1045\t  for lens in \"${lenses[@]}\"; do\n1046\t    provider=\"$(almanac_harden_role_field \"reviewer\" \"provider\" \"$lens\")\"\n1047\t    model=\"$(almanac_harden_role_field \"reviewer\" \"model\" \"$lens\")\"\n1048\t    effort=\"$(almanac_harden_role_field \"reviewer\" \"effort\" \"$lens\")\"\n1049\t\n1050\t    worker_id=\"reviewer-$lens\"\n1051\t    prompt_file=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/almanac-harden-prompt.XXXXXX\")\"\n1052\t    # Reviewers judge against the rubric when one exists (read gracefully when\n1053\t    # absent, e.g. an ad-hoc bare run with no drafted contract yet) and follow an\n1054\t    # operator steer directive when one was set at the HITL checkpoint.\n1055\t    almanac_harden_reviewer_prompt \"$target\" \"$lens\" \"$rubric_path\" \"$directive\" > \"$prompt_file\"\n1056\t\n1057\t    # Capture the worker pid via a file (not $(...)): worker_start backgrounds\n1058\t    # the agent as a child of THIS shell, so it stays waitable. A command\n1059\t    # substitution would reparent it into a subshell and break the wait.\n1060\t    pidfile=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/almanac-harden-pid.XXXXXX\")\"\n1061\t    almanac_loop_worker_start \"$root\" \"$run_id\" \"$worker_id\" \\\n1062\t      \"$provider\" \"$model\" \"$effort\" \"read-only\" \"$prompt_file\" > \"$pidfile\"\n1063\t    pid=\"$(cat \"$pidfile\")\"\n1064\t    rm -f \"$pidfile\"\n1065\t\n1066\t    worker_ids+=(\"$worker_id\")\n1067\t    worker_pids+=(\"$pid\")\n1068\t    prompt_files+=(\"$prompt_file\")\n1069\t    _info \"  reviewer lens=$lens provider=$provider pid=$pid (read-only)\"\n1070\t  done\n1071\t\n1072\t  # Reviewers run concurrently; block until every one finishes.\n1073\t  for pid in \"${worker_pids[@]}\"; do\n1074\t    wait \"$pid\" 2>/dev/null || true\n1075\t  done\n1076\t\n1077\t  total_added=0\n1078\t  succeeded_count=0\n1079\t  i=0\n1080\t  for worker_id in \"${worker_ids[@]}\"; do\n1081\t    lens=\"${lenses[$i]}\"\n1082\t    i=$((i + 1))\n1083\t    status_file=\"$(almanac_loop_worker_status_file \"$root\" \"$run_id\" \"$worker_id\")\"\n1084\t    result_file=\"$(almanac_loop_worker_file \"$root\" \"$run_id\" \"$worker_id\" \"result.txt\")\"\n1085\t\n1086\t    wstatus=\"\"\n1087\t    if [ -f \"$status_file\" ]; then\n1088\t      wstatus=\"$(almanac_loop_status_field \"$status_file\" \"status\" || true)\"\n1089\t    fi\n1090\t\n1091\t    if [ \"$wstatus\" != \"done\" ]; then\n1092\t      _warn \"reviewer lens=$lens failed or did not finish cleanly; skipping its findings\"\n1093\t      continue\n1094\t    fi\n1095\t    succeeded_count=$((succeeded_count + 1))\n1096\t\n1097\t    _info \"Findings (lens: $lens):\"\n1098\t    almanac_harden_format_findings \"$result_file\"\n1099\t\n1100\t    if [ -f \"$result_file\" ]; then\n1101\t      added=\"$(almanac_harden_ledger_record \"$ledger_path\" \"$result_file\" \"$round\")\"\n1102\t      total_added=$((total_added + added))\n1103\t    fi\n1104\t  done\n1105\t\n1106\t  [ \"${#prompt_files[@]}\" -eq 0 ] || rm -f \"${prompt_files[@]}\"\n1107\t\n1108\t  # Enforce the immutability invariant: revert (and warn about) any rubric edit\n1109\t  # an agent slipped in during the round.\n1110\t  if [ -n \"$rubric_snapshot\" ]; then\n1111\t    almanac_harden_rubric_verify \"$rubric_path\" \"$rubric_snapshot\" || true\n1112\t  fi\n1113\t\n1114\t  if [ \"$succeeded_count\" -eq 0 ]; then\n1115\t    _warn \"All reviewer workers failed; no reliable review result was produced.\"\n1116\t    return 1\n1117\t  fi\n1118\t\n1119\t  _success \"Aggregated $total_added new finding(s) into ${ledger_path#\"$root\"/}\"\n1120\t}\n1121\t\n1122\t# --- Single sequential fixer + feedback verdict --------------------------------\n1123\t#\n1124\t# After reviewers fan out and the conductor ratifies findings, ONE write-capable\n1125\t# fixer applies changes for the open blocking findings, in place, in the working\n1126\t# tree. v1 is deliberately a single sequential agent — no worktrees, no parallel\n1127\t# writers — so there is never a merge conflict to reconcile and any regression\n1128\t# test the fixer writes simply persists on disk. The fixer then runs the\n1129\t# project's feedback loops (shared detection + runner) and reports a verdict per\n1130\t# loop, so the objective half of \"bulletproof\" is enforced every round.\n1131\t\n1132\t# Build the prompt for the single sequential fixer. It receives the kill-list\n1133\t# (the open blocking findings) and the rubric bar, and is told to apply minimal\n1134\t# fixes AND leave a regression test per finding so the fix stays enforced. An\n1135\t# optional steering directive (4th arg) is embedded too, so a mid-run redirect at\n1136\t# the HITL checkpoint reaches the fixer. Exact wording is not asserted by tests by\n1137\t# design; that the fixer runs write-capable, its output persists, and it consumes\n1138\t# the steer directive is.\n1139\talmanac_harden_fixer_prompt() {\n1140\t  local target=\"$1\"\n1141\t  local findings_text=\"$2\"\n1142\t  local rubric_path=\"${3:-}\"\n1143\t  local directive=\"${4:-}\"\n1144\t  local rubric_bar=\"\"\n1145\t\n1146\t  if [ -n \"$rubric_path\" ] && [ -f \"$rubric_path\" ]; then\n1147\t    rubric_bar=\"$(almanac_harden_rubric_acceptance \"$rubric_path\")\"\n1148\t  fi\n1149\t\n1150\t  cat <<EOF\n1151\tYou are a single sequential fixer with write access to the repository. Apply the\n1152\tminimal changes that resolve every blocking finding below for the target. For\n1153\teach finding, add or update a regression test that fails before your fix and\n1154\tpasses after, so the defect cannot silently return.\n1155\t\n1156\tTarget: ${target}\n1157\t\n1158\tBlocking findings to fix:\n1159\t${findings_text}\n1160\tEOF\n1161\t\n1162\t  if [ -n \"$rubric_bar\" ]; then\n1163\t    cat <<EOF\n1164\t\n1165\tYour changes must satisfy this acceptance bar (the rubric contract):\n1166\t\n1167\t${rubric_bar}\n1168\tEOF\n1169\t  fi\n1170\t\n1171\t  if [ -n \"$directive\" ]; then\n1172\t    cat <<EOF\n1173\t\n1174\tThe operator steered this run with the directive below — apply it while you fix:\n1175\t\n1176\t${directive}\n1177\tEOF\n1178\t  fi\n1179\t\n1180\t  cat <<EOF\n1181\t\n1182\tDo not weaken, skip, or delete existing tests, and do not edit the rubric. Leave\n1183\tthe working tree building and the project's feedback loops (tests / typecheck /\n1184\tlint) green.\n1185\tEOF\n1186\t}\n1187\t\n1188\t# Run the single sequential fixer over the target's open blocking findings, then\n1189\t# run the project's feedback loops and report a pass/fail verdict per loop.\n1190\t#\n1191\t# One agent, write-capable (sandbox=workspace-write, NOT read-only), in place: no\n1192\t# worktree, so any regression tests it generates persist in the repo after the\n1193\t# run. Sequential by construction — a single foreground agent call — so there are\n1194\t# never concurrent writers. The fixer's agent call is bracketed by the rubric\n1195\t# immutability guard (snapshot before, verify after) so a write-capable fixer\n1196\t# cannot move the goalposts mid-run; legitimate rubric growth happens earlier, in\n1197\t# ratification, outside this bracket. On a clean fixer exit every open blocking\n1198\t# finding is marked `fixed` in the ledger; the next round's reviewers/ratify\n1199\t# reopen anything that still reproduces, so a still-broken finding cannot be\n1200\t# silently closed. A no-op (prints a note, returns 0) when there are no open\n1201\t# blocking findings. Returns the provider's exit code on a fixer failure, leaving\n1202\t# the findings open.\n1203\t#\n1204\t# The objective feedback gate is NOT run here: the convergence loop runs it once\n1205\t# per round (almanac_harden_round) so feedback executes every round even when\n1206\t# there is nothing to fix, and the gate reads a fresh verdict. The standalone\n1207\t# `--fix` CLI path runs almanac_harden_report_feedback explicitly afterwards.\n1208\talmanac_harden_fix() {\n1209\t  local root=\"$1\"\n1210\t  local target=\"$2\"\n1211\t  local round=\"${3:-1}\"\n1212\t  local directive=\"${4:-}\"\n1213\t  local target_path ledger_path rubric_path open findings_text count\n1214\t  local provider model effort prompt_file result_file events_file rubric_snapshot rc\n1215\t  local id lens severity location claim demonstration\n1216\t\n1217\t  case \"$target\" in\n1218\t    /*) target_path=\"$target\" ;;\n1219\t    *)  target_path=\"$root/$target\" ;;\n1220\t  esac\n1221\t\n1222\t  if [ ! -e \"$target_path\" ]; then\n1223\t    _die \"Harden target not found: $target\"\n1224\t  fi\n1225\t\n1226\t  ledger_path=\"$(almanac_harden_ledger_path \"$root\" \"$target\")\"\n1227\t  rubric_path=\"$(almanac_harden_rubric_path \"$root\" \"$target\")\"\n1228\t\n1229\t  open=\"$(almanac_harden_ledger_open_blocking \"$ledger_path\")\"\n1230\t  if [ -z \"$open\" ]; then\n1231\t    _info \"No open blocking findings to fix.\"\n1232\t    return 0\n1233\t  fi\n1234\t\n1235\t  count=\"$(printf '%s\\n' \"$open\" | grep -c .)\"\n1236\t\n1237\t  # Render the kill-list into the fixer prompt's findings block.\n1238\t  findings_text=\"$(\n1239\t    while IFS=$'\\t' read -r id lens severity location claim demonstration; do\n1240\t      [ -n \"$id\" ] || continue\n1241\t      printf -- '- [%s] %s: %s (at %s)\\n    demo: %s\\n' \\\n1242\t        \"${severity:-?}\" \"${lens:-?}\" \"${claim:-?}\" \"${location:-?}\" \"${demonstration:-?}\"\n1243\t    done <<INNER\n1244\t$open\n1245\tINNER\n1246\t  )\"\n1247\t\n1248\t  provider=\"$(almanac_harden_role_field \"fixer\" \"provider\")\"\n1249\t  model=\"$(almanac_harden_role_field \"fixer\" \"model\")\"\n1250\t  effort=\"$(almanac_harden_role_field \"fixer\" \"effort\")\"\n1251\t\n1252\t  prompt_file=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/almanac-harden-fixer-prompt.XXXXXX\")\"\n1253\t  result_file=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/almanac-harden-fixer-result.XXXXXX\")\"\n1254\t  events_file=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/almanac-harden-fixer-events.XXXXXX\")\"\n1255\t  almanac_harden_fixer_prompt \"$target\" \"$findings_text\" \"$rubric_path\" \"$directive\" > \"$prompt_file\"\n1256\t\n1257\t  # The rubric is immutable to agents during a run. The fixer is write-capable,\n1258\t  # so bracket its agent call: snapshot before, verify (revert + warn) after.\n1259\t  rubric_snapshot=\"\"\n1260\t  if [ -f \"$rubric_path\" ]; then\n1261\t    rubric_snapshot=\"$(almanac_harden_rubric_snapshot \"$rubric_path\")\" || rubric_snapshot=\"\"\n1262\t  fi\n1263\t\n1264\t  _info \"Fixing $count open blocking finding(s) with one sequential fixer (provider=$provider, write-capable)\"\n1265\t\n1266\t  rc=0\n1267\t  almanac_loop_agent_capture \"$provider\" \"$model\" \"$effort\" \"workspace-write\" \\\n1268\t    \"$prompt_file\" \"$result_file\" \"$events_file\" >/dev/null || rc=$?\n1269\t\n1270\t  rm -f \"$prompt_file\" \"$result_file\" \"$events_file\"\n1271\t\n1272\t  if [ -n \"$rubric_snapshot\" ]; then\n1273\t    almanac_harden_rubric_verify \"$rubric_path\" \"$rubric_snapshot\" || true\n1274\t  fi\n1275\t\n1276\t  if [ \"$rc\" -ne 0 ]; then\n1277\t    _warn \"Fixer failed (exit $rc); blocking findings remain open.\"\n1278\t    return \"$rc\"\n1279\t  fi\n1280\t\n1281\t  # The single fixer addresses the whole kill-list; mark all open blocking\n1282\t  # findings fixed in one ledger rewrite. A finding that still reproduces is\n1283\t  # reopened next round.\n1284\t  printf '%s\\n' \"$open\" | awk -F '\\t' '$1 != \"\" { print $1 }' \\\n1285\t    | almanac_harden_ledger_set_status_many \"$ledger_path\" \"fixed\" \\\n1286\t      \"fixed by sequential fixer at round $round\"\n1287\t\n1288\t  _success \"Applied fixes for $count finding(s); regenerated tests persist in the working tree.\"\n1289\t}\n1290\t\n1291\t# Run the project's feedback loops via the shared runner and print a pass/fail\n1292\t# verdict per loop. Returns the runner's aggregate (0 = all green, non-zero =\n1293\t# any failed) so a caller (the convergence gate, later) can act on it.\n1294\talmanac_harden_report_feedback() {\n1295\t  local root=\"$1\"\n1296\t  local verdicts cmd verdict rc\n1297\t\n1298\t  _info \"Running project feedback loops:\"\n1299\t\n1300\t  rc=0\n1301\t  verdicts=\"$(almanac_loop_feedback_run \"$root\")\" || rc=$?\n1302\t\n1303\t  if [ -z \"$verdicts\" ]; then\n1304\t    _info \"  (no feedback loops detected)\"\n1305\t    return 0\n1306\t  fi\n1307\t\n1308\t  while IFS=$'\\t' read -r cmd verdict; do\n1309\t    [ -n \"$cmd\" ] || continue\n1310\t    if [ \"$verdict\" = \"pass\" ]; then\n1311\t      _success \"  PASS  $cmd\"\n1312\t    else\n1313\t      _warn \"  FAIL  $cmd\"\n1314\t    fi\n1315\t  done <<INNER\n1316\t$verdicts\n1317\tINNER\n1318\t\n1319\t  return \"$rc\"\n1320\t}\n1321\t\n1322\t# --- Convergence loop + gate ---------------------------------------------------\n1323\t#\n1324\t# A round is the full hardening pass over one target: fan out reviewers, ratify\n1325\t# their findings by execution, fix the blocking ones, and run the project's\n1326\t# feedback loops. The convergence loop repeats rounds until the gate says stop:\n1327\t# it converges when the acceptance bar is met AND no open blocking findings\n1328\t# remain, gives up with a clear NON-CONVERGED status when the round budget is\n1329\t# hit, and otherwise checks in with the human (ship vs. continue) between rounds.\n1330\t# Because the gate only ever exits on convergence or the budget, the loop always\n1331\t# terminates — a pathological target cannot run forever.\n1332\t\n1333\t# Pure convergence predicate. Given the round's state, decide what the loop does\n1334\t# next. No I/O, no side effects (besides echoing the verdict) so it is trivially\n1335\t# unit-testable across the whole input space:\n1336\t#\n1337\t#   acceptance_met  1 = every acceptance criterion is met, else 0\n1338\t#   open_blocking   count of open blocking findings still remaining\n1339\t#   round           the round that just finished (1-based)\n1340\t#   budget          the hard round cap (>= 1)\n1341\t#"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RmrkhyD6hi6hJV8qXrRsBk","session_id":"048450e6-ddc8-4b99-9d57-06daabf0abc2","uuid":"a40ae355-4b65-4494-9381-d1e8d7b8cb18","timestamp":"2026-05-27T06:02:09.814Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Find architectural friction in lib"}
