{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BsbWjRgemsozC5fmJgU4Xi","type":"tool_result","content":"820\t# as \"not\", so an un-parseable verdict is conservatively a non-blocking note.\n821\talmanac_harden_ratify_verdict() {\n822\t  local result_file=\"$1\"\n823\t\n824\t  [ -f \"$result_file\" ] || { printf '%s\\n' \"not\"; return 0; }\n825\t\n826\t  if grep -Fxq 'HARDEN_VERDICT=reproduces' \"$result_file\" 2>/dev/null; then\n827\t    printf '%s\\n' \"reproduces\"\n828\t  else\n829\t    printf '%s\\n' \"not\"\n830\t  fi\n831\t}\n832\t\n833\t# Execution seam: decide whether a finding's demonstration reproduces against the\n834\t# target. Return 0 = reproduces (real defect, blocking), non-zero = does not\n835\t# reproduce (opinion / stale). This seam IS the conductor executing the\n836\t# demonstration: it runs the demonstration through the resolved conductor provider\n837\t# (the (provider, model, effort) it is handed — no host-marker dependence, so it\n838\t# is mixable per the role config) via the shared agent runner and reads the\n839\t# conductor's verdict back from its final message. PRD story 8: \"blocking means\n840\t# objectively reproducible, not a reviewer's assertion.\"\n841\t#\n842\t# Conservative on every uncertainty so opinions never silently gate the loop and\n843\t# a flaky/missing provider never blocks a run: an empty demonstration, an\n844\t# unresolved conductor provider, a failed/un-runnable conductor call, or an\n845\t# un-parseable verdict all read as non-reproducing (a note). Tests override this\n846\t# to drive the decision paths directly; here it is the real executor.\n847\talmanac_harden_demo_reproduces() {\n848\t  local demonstration=\"$1\"\n849\t  local target_path=\"${2:-}\"\n850\t  local conductor_provider=\"${3:-}\"\n851\t  local conductor_model=\"${4:-}\"\n852\t  local conductor_effort=\"${5:-}\"\n853\t  local prompt_file result_file events_file verdict rc\n854\t\n855\t  # Nothing to execute / no provider to execute it through -> conservative note.\n856\t  [ -n \"$demonstration\" ] || return 1\n857\t  [ -n \"$conductor_provider\" ] || return 1\n858\t\n859\t  prompt_file=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/almanac-harden-ratify-prompt.XXXXXX\")\" || return 1\n860\t  result_file=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/almanac-harden-ratify-result.XXXXXX\")\" || { rm -f \"$prompt_file\"; return 1; }\n861\t  events_file=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/almanac-harden-ratify-events.XXXXXX\")\" || { rm -f \"$prompt_file\" \"$result_file\"; return 1; }\n862\t\n863\t  almanac_harden_ratify_prompt \"$demonstration\" \"$target_path\" > \"$prompt_file\"\n864\t\n865\t  # Reviewer text is untrusted. Ratification may inspect/run existing repro\n866\t  # commands, but it must not write to the repo before the single fixer phase.\n867\t  rc=0\n868\t  almanac_loop_agent_capture \"$conductor_provider\" \"$conductor_model\" \"$conductor_effort\" \\\n869\t    \"read-only\" \"$prompt_file\" \"$result_file\" \"$events_file\" >/dev/null 2>&1 || rc=$?\n870\t\n871\t  if [ \"$rc\" -ne 0 ]; then\n872\t    # Provider missing/crashed or the demonstration was un-runnable: cannot\n873\t    # confirm reproduction -> non-blocking note, never a hang or a hard failure.\n874\t    rm -f \"$prompt_file\" \"$result_file\" \"$events_file\"\n875\t    return 1\n876\t  fi\n877\t\n878\t  verdict=\"$(almanac_harden_ratify_verdict \"$result_file\")\"\n879\t  rm -f \"$prompt_file\" \"$result_file\" \"$events_file\"\n880\t\n881\t  [ \"$verdict\" = \"reproduces\" ] && return 0\n882\t  return 1\n883\t}\n884\t\n885\t# Adjudicate one finding by executing its demonstration through the seam and\n886\t# recording the outcome in the ledger. Prints the verdict:\n887\t#   blocking - new/open finding whose demonstration reproduces (ratified, gates)\n888\t#   note     - new/open finding that does not reproduce (non-blocking note)\n889\t#   reopened - an already-adjudicated finding whose demonstration newly reproduces\n890\t#   dropped  - an already-adjudicated finding that still does not reproduce\n891\t# Already-adjudicated findings are re-litigated ONLY when they newly reproduce,\n892\t# so a rejected opinion cannot churn the loop round after round.\n893\t#\n894\t# When a rubric path is given, a finding that reproduces (blocking or reopened)\n895\t# also appends a falsifiable criterion to the rubric's `## Acceptance` — the bar\n896\t# grows monotonically and visibly with every ratified defect. Notes and drops\n897\t# never touch the rubric, so opinions cannot raise the bar.\n898\t#\n899\t# The trailing conductor (provider, model, effort) args (11th-13th) identify the\n900\t# provider that executes the demonstration; they are passed straight to the\n901\t# execution seam. Optional/backward-compatible — omit them to use the default.\n902\talmanac_harden_ratify() {\n903\t  local path=\"$1\"\n904\t  local id=\"$2\"\n905\t  local lens=\"$3\"\n906\t  local severity=\"$4\"\n907\t  local location=\"$5\"\n908\t  local claim=\"$6\"\n909\t  local demonstration=\"$7\"\n910\t  local round=\"${8:-1}\"\n911\t  local target_path=\"${9:-}\"\n912\t  local rubric_path=\"${10:-}\"\n913\t  local conductor_provider=\"${11:-}\"\n914\t  local conductor_model=\"${12:-}\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"048450e6-ddc8-4b99-9d57-06daabf0abc2","uuid":"38cfaade-946b-49ad-a746-82b93926b2ed","timestamp":"2026-05-27T06:06:01.929Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/jakubneumann/Documents/code/neumie/almanac/lib/harden-core.sh","content":"# as \"not\", so an un-parseable verdict is conservatively a non-blocking note.\nalmanac_harden_ratify_verdict() {\n  local result_file=\"$1\"\n\n  [ -f \"$result_file\" ] || { printf '%s\\n' \"not\"; return 0; }\n\n  if grep -Fxq 'HARDEN_VERDICT=reproduces' \"$result_file\" 2>/dev/null; then\n    printf '%s\\n' \"reproduces\"\n  else\n    printf '%s\\n' \"not\"\n  fi\n}\n\n# Execution seam: decide whether a finding's demonstration reproduces against the\n# target. Return 0 = reproduces (real defect, blocking), non-zero = does not\n# reproduce (opinion / stale). This seam IS the conductor executing the\n# demonstration: it runs the demonstration through the resolved conductor provider\n# (the (provider, model, effort) it is handed — no host-marker dependence, so it\n# is mixable per the role config) via the shared agent runner and reads the\n# conductor's verdict back from its final message. PRD story 8: \"blocking means\n# objectively reproducible, not a reviewer's assertion.\"\n#\n# Conservative on every uncertainty so opinions never silently gate the loop and\n# a flaky/missing provider never blocks a run: an empty demonstration, an\n# unresolved conductor provider, a failed/un-runnable conductor call, or an\n# un-parseable verdict all read as non-reproducing (a note). Tests override this\n# to drive the decision paths directly; here it is the real executor.\nalmanac_harden_demo_reproduces() {\n  local demonstration=\"$1\"\n  local target_path=\"${2:-}\"\n  local conductor_provider=\"${3:-}\"\n  local conductor_model=\"${4:-}\"\n  local conductor_effort=\"${5:-}\"\n  local prompt_file result_file events_file verdict rc\n\n  # Nothing to execute / no provider to execute it through -> conservative note.\n  [ -n \"$demonstration\" ] || return 1\n  [ -n \"$conductor_provider\" ] || return 1\n\n  prompt_file=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/almanac-harden-ratify-prompt.XXXXXX\")\" || return 1\n  result_file=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/almanac-harden-ratify-result.XXXXXX\")\" || { rm -f \"$prompt_file\"; return 1; }\n  events_file=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/almanac-harden-ratify-events.XXXXXX\")\" || { rm -f \"$prompt_file\" \"$result_file\"; return 1; }\n\n  almanac_harden_ratify_prompt \"$demonstration\" \"$target_path\" > \"$prompt_file\"\n\n  # Reviewer text is untrusted. Ratification may inspect/run existing repro\n  # commands, but it must not write to the repo before the single fixer phase.\n  rc=0\n  almanac_loop_agent_capture \"$conductor_provider\" \"$conductor_model\" \"$conductor_effort\" \\\n    \"read-only\" \"$prompt_file\" \"$result_file\" \"$events_file\" >/dev/null 2>&1 || rc=$?\n\n  if [ \"$rc\" -ne 0 ]; then\n    # Provider missing/crashed or the demonstration was un-runnable: cannot\n    # confirm reproduction -> non-blocking note, never a hang or a hard failure.\n    rm -f \"$prompt_file\" \"$result_file\" \"$events_file\"\n    return 1\n  fi\n\n  verdict=\"$(almanac_harden_ratify_verdict \"$result_file\")\"\n  rm -f \"$prompt_file\" \"$result_file\" \"$events_file\"\n\n  [ \"$verdict\" = \"reproduces\" ] && return 0\n  return 1\n}\n\n# Adjudicate one finding by executing its demonstration through the seam and\n# recording the outcome in the ledger. Prints the verdict:\n#   blocking - new/open finding whose demonstration reproduces (ratified, gates)\n#   note     - new/open finding that does not reproduce (non-blocking note)\n#   reopened - an already-adjudicated finding whose demonstration newly reproduces\n#   dropped  - an already-adjudicated finding that still does not reproduce\n# Already-adjudicated findings are re-litigated ONLY when they newly reproduce,\n# so a rejected opinion cannot churn the loop round after round.\n#\n# When a rubric path is given, a finding that reproduces (blocking or reopened)\n# also appends a falsifiable criterion to the rubric's `## Acceptance` — the bar\n# grows monotonically and visibly with every ratified defect. Notes and drops\n# never touch the rubric, so opinions cannot raise the bar.\n#\n# The trailing conductor (provider, model, effort) args (11th-13th) identify the\n# provider that executes the demonstration; they are passed straight to the\n# execution seam. Optional/backward-compatible — omit them to use the default.\nalmanac_harden_ratify() {\n  local path=\"$1\"\n  local id=\"$2\"\n  local lens=\"$3\"\n  local severity=\"$4\"\n  local location=\"$5\"\n  local claim=\"$6\"\n  local demonstration=\"$7\"\n  local round=\"${8:-1}\"\n  local target_path=\"${9:-}\"\n  local rubric_path=\"${10:-}\"\n  local conductor_provider=\"${11:-}\"\n  local conductor_model=\"${12:-}\"","numLines":95,"startLine":820,"totalLines":1980}}}
